`applyStyle` has `r` and calls `applyStringProperty(el, propId, text)` / `applyNumericProperty(el, propId, valueType, op.c)` without `r`. I'll route the media property handling through `applyStyle` so it has `r`. The cleanest: add the media prop cases in `applyStyle` (which has `r`) BEFORE the generic applyNumericProperty fallthrough, OR pass `r` into applyNumericProperty. 

Simplest: handle the 3 media numeric props in `applyStyle` (it has `r`) — but they're numeric; applyStyle's SET_PROPERTY branch splits by valueType. PLAYBACK_STATE is U32, MEDIA_POSITION/VOLUME are F32 — both numeric (not VAL_STRING/VAL_DESIGN_TOKEN), so they'd fall to `applyNumericProperty`. Let me add a media branch in `applyStyle` before the numeric fallthrough:

```ts
} else if (propId === PROP_PLAYBACK_STATE || propId === PROP_MEDIA_POSITION || propId === PROP_MEDIA_VOLUME) {
  applyMediaProperty(el, r, propId, valueType, op.c);
}
```

And `applyMediaProperty(el, r, propId, valueType, bits)`:
- find the media element (mediaElementOf).
- setupMedia(el, r) (attach listeners).
- PLAYBACK_STATE: playing = (valueType === VAL_U8 ? bits & 0xff : bits) !== 0; if playing media.play() else media.pause(); mark suppression.
- MEDIA_POSITION: media.currentTime = f32FromBits(bits); set suppressTimeUntil.
- MEDIA_VOLUME: media.volume = clamp(f32FromBits(bits)); mark suppression.
- finalizeNative(el): if the node element is a `.pathland-media` wrapper with no children besides the media → set media.controls = true.

Wait — the `applyNumericProperty` also calls `applyProperty(el, propId, ...)` for generic handling (which sets style props). The media props aren't style props; they shouldn't go through `applyProperty` generic. So routing them to `applyMediaProperty` and NOT to applyNumericProperty is right.

Also — AUDIO_SOURCE/VIDEO_SOURCE (string props) currently handled in applyStringProperty. I should also call setupMedia + finalizeNative there. Let me update applyStringProperty's AUDIO_SOURCE/VIDEO_SOURCE cases to also setup media. But applyStringProperty doesn't have `r`. Hmm. The source is applied during SET_PROPERTY in applyStyle which has `r`. So better: handle AUDIO_SOURCE/VIDEO_SOURCE in applyStyle too (before the generic applyStringProperty call). Let me restructure: in applyStyle's SET_PROPERTY branch, add:

```ts
if (valueType === VAL_STRING) {
  const text = readString(strings, op.c);
  if (propId === PROP_ROUTE) { ... }
  else if (propId === PROP_AUDIO_SOURCE || propId === PROP_VIDEO_SOURCE) {
    applyStringProperty(el, propId, text);
    setupMediaElement(el, r);
    finalizeNativeMedia(el);
  } else { applyStringProperty(el, propId, text); }
}
```

And for the numeric media props:
```ts
} else if (propId === PROP_PLAYBACK_STATE || propId === PROP_MEDIA_POSITION || propId === PROP_MEDIA_VOLUME) {
  applyMediaProperty(el, r, propId, valueType, op.c);
}
```

Let me write the media helper functions at the end of apply.ts:
- `mediaElementOf(el)`.
- `mediaState` WeakMap + `setupMediaElement(el, r)`.
- `applyMediaProperty(el, r, propId, valueType, bits)`.
- `finalizeNativeMedia(el)`.

The setupMediaElement attaches listeners to the media element:
```ts
const mediaState = new WeakMap<HTMLMediaElement, { suppressTimeUntil: number; suppressUntil: number }>();

function mediaElementOf(el: HTMLElement): HTMLMediaElement | null {
  return el.matches("audio,video")
    ? (el as HTMLMediaElement)
    : el.querySelector<HTMLMediaElement>("audio,video");
}

function setupMediaElement(el: HTMLElement, r: DomRenderer): void {
  const media = mediaElementOf(el);
  if (!media) return;
  if (mediaState.has(media)) return; // already wired
  const state = { suppressTimeUntil: 0, suppressUntil: 0 };
  mediaState.set(media, state);
  const id = Number(el.getAttribute("data-pathland-id"));
  const send = r.onMediaEvent;
  if (!send) return;
  const sendIfNotSuppressed = (batch: Uint8Array, now: number, timeWindow: number) => {
    if (now < state.suppressUntil) return;
    void batch; void timeWindow;
    send(batch);
  };
  media.addEventListener("play", () => {
    const now = performance.now();
    if (now < state.suppressUntil) return;
    send(encodeMediaPlayStateChanged(id, true));
  });
  media.addEventListener("pause", () => {
    const now = performance.now();
    if (now < state.suppressUntil) return;
    send(encodeMediaPlayStateChanged(id, false));
  });
  media.addEventListener("timeupdate", () => {
    const now = performance.now();
    if (now < state.suppressTimeUntil) return;
    send(encodeMediaTimeUpdated(id, media.currentTime));
  });
  media.addEventListener("ended", () => {
    send(encodeMediaEnded(id));
  });
  media.addEventListener("volumechange", () => {
    const now = performance.now();
    if (now < state.suppressUntil) return;
    send(encodeMediaVolumeChanged(id, media.volume));
  });
